":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d57\"},\"ref\":\"d57\",\"snippet\":\" ... the likes of US-based Nigerian Booker Prize shortlistee Chigozie Obioma to take on the mantle of bootstrap race \\\"analysis\\\" in a more sophisticated manner. A few months before the 2016 Aké Festival Black Lives Matter panel, Obioma saw it fit to make his intervention into the debate ... \",\"title\":\"https://africasacountry.com/2019/04/why-im-no-longer-talking-to-nigerians-about-race\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d6\"},\"ref\":\"d6\",\"snippet\":\" ... In the 21st century the average number of books considered by the judges has been approximately 130.\\n\\nRelated awards for translated works\\n\\nA separate prize for which any living writer in the world may qualify, the Man Booker International Prize, was inaugurated in 2005. Until 2015, it was ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"df8b6bdd0de6780867076ac0d84f290a3525eac3964578d56912d32f06f4b10c\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"0f387d10e2b7c9c19c1b79eacba572e2f75c257c2a51fe1815b019038bb2e611\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"The Fishermen Chigozie Obioma 2015 Booker shortlist translated languages\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d74\"},\"ref\":\"d74\",\"snippet\":\" ... Lourdes Maria Ciccone Leon (born 1996)\\n\\n- With Guy Ritchie: Rocco Ritchie (born 2000)\\n\\n- Adopted as a single mother: David Banda (adopted 2006), Mercy James (adopted 2009), twins Esther and Stella Mwale (adopted 2017)\\n\\n- Age: 66\\n\\n- Birthplace: Michigan, USA, Bay City\\n\\nOzzy Osbourne has six children with two different ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.ranker.com/list/rock-stars-with-the-most-kids/celebrity-lists\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d75\"},\"ref\":\"d75\",\"snippet\":\" ... 95 years, 6 months, and 9 days\\n\\nBirthplace: Minneapolis, Minnesota, USA\\n\\nYears Active: 1945 – Present\\n\\nNotable Works: Big Trouble in Little China, Blade Runner, Kung Fu Panda\\n\\nphoto source: Wikimedia Commons\\n\\nJames Hong is renowned for his extensive contributions to film and television, appearing in over 600 roles ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oldest.org/culture/living-actors/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d76\"},\"ref\":\"d76\",\"snippet\":\" ... Born in Great Bend, Kansas, Allyson now lives in New York City, after growing up in Omaha, Nebraska and earning her bachelor's degree in Piano Performance from the University of Nebraska at Omaha. She spent time in both Kansas City and Minneapolis before making the move in ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.nojc.org/sandbar\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d77\"},\"ref\":\"d77\",\"snippet\":\" ... Barry Keoghan\\n\\nBORN: October 18, 1992\\n\\nBIRTHPLACE: Dublin, Ireland\\n\\nCHILD: Brando\\n\\nASTROLOGICAL SIGN: Libra\\n\\nEarly Life\\n\\nBarry Keoghan was born on October 18, 1992, and raised in the Summerhill neighborhood of Dublin. Keoghan had no relationship with his father, whose identity hasn't been made public. His mother ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.biography.com/actors/a46180093/barry-keoghan\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d78\"},\"ref\":\"d78\",\"snippet\":\" ... Michael Joseph Jackson\\n\\nBORN: August 29, 1958\\n\\nDIED: June 25, 2009\\n\\nBIRTHPLACE: Gary, Indiana\\n\\nSPOUSES: Lisa Marie Presley (1994-1996) and Debbie Rowe (1996-2000)\\n\\nCHILDREN: Michael \\\"Prince,\\\" Paris, and Prince \\\"Blanket\\\"\\n\\nASTROLOGICAL SIGN: Virgo\\n\\nEarly Life and Family\\n\\nMichael Joseph Jackson was born on August 29, 1958 ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.biography.com/musicians/michael-jackson\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d79\"},\"ref\":\"d79\",\"snippet\":\" ... Francis Ford Coppola\\n\\nBORN: April 7, 1939\\n\\nBIRTHPLACE: Detroit, Michigan\\n\\nSPOUSE: Eleanor Coppola (1963-2024)\\n\\nCHILDREN: Gian-Carlo, Roman, and Sofia Coppola\\n\\nASTROLOGICAL SIGN: Aries\\n\\nEarly Life\\n\\nFrancis Ford Coppola was born on April 7, 1939, in Detroit. Stricken with polio as a child, he was bedridden and ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.biography.com/movies-tv/francis-ford-coppola\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d80\"},\"ref\":\"d80\",\"snippet\":\" ... Ninna Priscilla Brando (born May 13, 1989), Myles Jonathan Brando (born January 16, 1992) and Timothy Gahan Brando (born January 6, 1994). Brando also adopted Petra Brando-Corval (born 1972), the daughter of his assistant Caroline Barrett and novelist James Clavell.Heller, Matthew. \\\"Brando Will Left Zilch For ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marlon_Brando\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d81\"},\"ref\":\"d81\",\"snippet\":\" ... Turning professional, Marlon put together a band and began to book himself gigs at concerts and local clubs.\\n\\nA year later, a friend brought him a video which featured Dizzy Gillespie, Chick Corea, Miroslav Vitous and others and his love for Jazz was born. Marlon became seduced by ... \",\"title\":\"https://latinjazznet.com/artist-profiles/marlon-simon/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d82\"},\"ref\":\"d82\",\"snippet\":\" ... She loves her city and would do anything to save its people. This is, in fact, the plan for her life, made before she was even born. Her brother, Bador, is a small monkey bot with a big attitude and bigger ambitions. He wants a chance to leave ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.richlandlibrary.com/staff-picks/broader-bookshelf-2025-read-science-fiction-novel-bipoc-author\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d83\"},\"ref\":\"d83\",\"snippet\":\" ... 6/9\\n\\nMarlon Jackson\\n\\nMarlon David Jackson, 67, was born on March 12, 1957 and was also part of The Jackson 5. His twin, Brandon Jackson, passed away within hours of his birth. In addition to a solo music career, he also pursued a career in real estate ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.hellomagazine.com/celebrities/718597/meet-jackson-family-children-michael-jackson-siblings/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"7f209f7c93b5d530271b3125e649a1ea1dff08f84a9dc84f8bdef1e92d618681\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"4ffa0bb7cecfa3fa1dcb8038544a510fe3615808b596f8501de3a7d30d2f8ed9\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Marlon James born birthplace city\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_f9747ad8252c4eb5ae3a73fd"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"evidence\":{\"document\":\"d38\",\"document_chars\":17355,\"end\":3000,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e1\",\"sha256\":\"79767844ce2071fc5dcf3fb0e64d0cade0ba154ef0fc324d0054c1c767e63138\",\"snapshot\":\"90019ca46504785f620ef12f36abae20080c8c3bc7809053339e4beaa4deb2fd\",\"start\":0,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: ADVISORS\\ndate: 2022-01-01\\n---\\nADVISORS\\n\\nAdvisors\\n\\nProgram Director\\n\\nChigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationalerpris, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated for two dozen prizes for fiction. He was named one of Foreign Policy's 100 Leading Global Thinkers in 2015 and served as a judge of the Booker prize in 2021. He is the Helen S. Lanier Distinguished Professor of English and Creative Writing at the University of Georgia, and the program director of the Oxbelly Writers retreat. His third novel, The Road to the Country, was published in 2024.\\n\\nProgram Manager\\n\\nRosie is a production and event manager based in Athens, Greece, with extensive experience in coordinating high-profile film festivals and cultural events. She holds a degree in Communication, Media and Culture from Athens and pursued further studies in Art History in Paris, culminating in a Master's in Culture & Tourism from Université Paris 1 Panthéon-Sorbonne. Her professional experience includes collaborations with cultural organizations and festivals worldwide, including UNESCO in New York, the Rolex Art Festival, Les Rencontres d'Arles Photo Festival among others. Since 2018, she has served as Festival Coordinator and Special Events Manager for the French Film Festival of Greece, and since 2022, she has been the Head of Production for the Athens International Children's Film Festival. Driven by a deep passion for cultural engagement and sustainable tourism, she continually seeks innovative ways to connect communities through the arts. In her free time, she enjoys playing music and gardening.\\n\\nProgram Director\\n\\nChigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationaler Literaturpreis, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated for two dozen prizes for fiction. He was a judge of the Booker prize in 2021. He is the Helen S. Lanier Professor of Creative Writing and English at the University of Georgia, and the program director of the Oxbelly Fiction Writers program. His third novel, The Road to the Country, will be published in 2024.\\n\\nProgram Manager\\n\\nKaterina Papanikolopoulos joined Faliro House in 2022 as Manager of Special Projects – a position that evolved into her role acting as the 2024 Oxbelly Retreat, Fiction Writers Program Manager. Following her graduation from UCLA (Summa Cum Laude, Art History), Papanikolopoulos founded the non-profit Athens Design Forum (ADF), a platform that advocates for overlooked and generative design histories interwoven with global labor and migration pa\"},\"executed\":true,\"next_start\":3000,\"ok\":true,\"previously_received\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_eff7df42204b484ba21c860a"},{"content":"I now have strong evidence. Let me verify the key connection: Marlon James (2015 Booker winner) was born in Kingston, Jamaica, and Chigozie Obioma grew up in Akure, Nigeria. The question states the prize-winning author was born in the same city where the first author grew up. Let me confirm Marlon James's birthplace and that Obioma grew up in Akure.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Marlon James born Kingston Jamaica\", \"Chigozie Obioma grew up Akure Nigeria childhood\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_9ef4fe5a56b34c3d9bc8aac4","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d84\"},\"ref\":\"d84\",\"snippet\":\" ... James in the 82nd minute to replace Je-Vaughn Watson. The former Kingston College schoolboy and Harbour View's under-21 player, entered the game and within minutes hit a sensational volleyed home from a right-sided cross from Ryan Johnson from inside the area to earn Jamaica ... \",\"title\":\"https://thereggaeboyz.com/news.htm\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d85\"},\"ref\":\"d85\",\"snippet\":\" ... Born in Kingston, Jamaica, W.I., one of 5 children of Simon and Najla Brimo. Juliette married beloved husband James H. Bryant in 1956 and immigrated to the U.S. and Ft. Lauderdale. She is survived by her two sons, James N. of Orlando and Michael F. of ... \",\"title\":\"http://www.jamaicanfamilysearch.com/Samples/elsewher.htm\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d86\"},\"ref\":\"d86\",\"snippet\":\" ... Contributor\\n\\nMarlon James was born in Kingston, Jamaica. His work has been exhibited at the National Gallery of Jamaica, the IDB Cultural Center (DC), Art Museum of Americas (DC), Bargehouse (London), and Aliceyard (Trinidad).\",\"title\":\"https://strangersguide.com/articles/king-yellowman/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d87\"},\"ref\":\"d87\",\"snippet\":\" ... 107–123.\\n* Michener, James, A. 1989. Caribbean (especially Chap. XI. \\\"Martial Law in Jamaica\\\", pp. 403–442. Semi-fictional but mainly accurate). London: Secker & Warburg. .\\n* Morales Padrón, Francisco. 1953 2003. Spanish Jamaica. Kingston: Ian Randle Publishers.\\n* Nelson, Charmaine A. 2017. Slavery, geography and empire in nineteenth-century marine ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Jamaica\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d88\"},\"ref\":\"d88\",\"snippet\":\" ... Business venture\\n\\nIn 2009, Spice launched her clothing boutique chain Spicey Couture in Jamaica. The chain had branches in Kingston, May Pen and Montego Bay. As of 2020, the chain is no longer active.\\n\\nIn 2010, Spice opened a beauty salon called Spicey Salon in Kingston. She also ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spice_(musician)\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d89\"},\"ref\":\"d89\",\"snippet\":\" ... A Man on the Inside premieres 21 November on Netflix internationally\\n\\nGet Millie Black\\n\\nThe Jamaican-born novelist Marlon James, whose books include the Booker Prize winner A Brief History of Seven Killings (2014) and the Africa-set fantasy Black Leopard, Red Wolf (2019) created this crime series ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.bbc.com/culture/article/20241028-11-of-the-best-tv-shows-to-watch-this-november\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d90\"},\"ref\":\"d90\",\"snippet\":\" ... A Brief History of Seven Killings, by Marlon James\\n\\nA nightmare symphony of crime that begins in 1970s Jamaica and never really leaves, even as the semi-historical plot leaves a surreal blood trail from a Bob Marley assassination attempt to crack-addled New York City. James' intoxicating ... \",\"title\":\"https://ew.com/books/2019/11/25/best-of-the-decade-top-10-fiction-books/?srsltid=AfmBOop0ufKoVqU4RELY55P6eS3L4rXFZLCabqalM9VtLWkrcVEOOLAO\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d91\"},\"ref\":\"d91\",\"snippet\":\" ... Akin's impressive acting career includes his memorable role as Charlie DeSalvo in the cult classic television series Highlander, solidifying him as one of Jamaica's most iconic TV actors.\\n\\n- Birthplace: Kingston, Jamaica\\n\\n- Nationality: Canada, Jamaica\\n\\nBorn in Christiana, Jamaica, Roger Cross has become a household name in ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.ranker.com/list/famous-tv-actors-from-jamaica/reference\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d92\"},\"ref\":\"d92\",\"snippet\":\" ... Old Bill\\\"), born in Murree, India,1888.\\n\\n• George Baker, British Actor, born in Bulgaria\\n\\n• James.G. Ballard, British Fiction Writer, born in Shanghai, China,1930.\\n\\n• Victor Barna, British Table-Tennis Champion, born in Hungary\\n\\n• Peter Simon Barnes, England Football International (22 Caps), born in Kingston, Jamaica, 1957.\\n\\n• Lord ... \",\"title\":\"https://peek-01.livejournal.com/64479.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d93\"},\"ref\":\"d93\",\"snippet\":\" ... These are the stories that we never believed could be told, until Jonathan Escoffery told them.\\\" ―Marlon James, author of Moon Witch, Spider King\\n\\n\\\"Profound, tender, and laugh-out-loud hilarious, If I Survive You will knock you off your feet and keep you spellbound to the very ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.amazon.com/If-Survive-You-Jonathan-Escoffery/dp/037460598X\"