advanced by endless protests or marches of \\\"equality\\\" or \\\"justice.\\\"\\n\\nAfter dismissing the necessity of protest in struggle, Obioma goes on to hold up his country of birth Nigeria as an example ... \",\"title\":\"https://africasacountry.com/2019/04/why-im-no-longer-talking-to-nigerians-about-race\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d53\"},\"ref\":\"d53\",\"snippet\":\" ... Farrell\\n*Karen Joy Fowler\\n*Linda Grant\\n*Abdulrazak Gurnah\\n*Sarah Hall\\n*Mohsin Hamid\\n*Shirley Hazzard\\n*Philip Hensher\\n*Mary Lawson\\n*David Lodge\\n*Patrick McCabe\\n*Colum McCann\\n*Tom McCarthy\\n*Shena Mackay\\n*Chigozie Obioma\\n*Michael Ondaatje\\n*Joseph O'Neill\\n*Tim Parks\\n*Caryl Phillips\\n*Julian Rathbone\\n*Mordecai Richler\\n*Arundhati Roy\\n*Bernice Rubens\\n*Donal ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d58\"},\"ref\":\"d58\",\"snippet\":\" ... Chigozie Obioma\\ndate: 2000-01-01\\n---\\n-\\n\\n- MajorsMinorsCertificates\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Policies & ProceduresFYW Guidebook\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Digital Learning LabsPortfoliosEvaluationsMoran ePortfolio AwardsBarnett Essay AwardsDouble Dawgs\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Transfer FAQProspective Student Information\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Study AbroadInternships and Research Opportunities\\n\\n>>\\n\\n-\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Double DawgsTransfer Student InformationDual Degree Progra\",\"title\":\"https://www.english.uga.edu/directory/people/chigozie-obioma\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d56\"},\"ref\":\"d56\",\"snippet\":\" ... Oromay (\\\"The End\\\")\\n* Chinua Achebe (Nigeria): Arrow of God (1964), No Longer At Ease (1960), Things Fall Apart (1958), A Man of the People (1966), Anthills of the Savannah (1987), \\n* Chimamanda Ngozi Adichie (Nigeria): Purple Hibiscus (2003), Half of a Yellow Sun (2006), Americanah (2013)\\n* Chigozie Obioma (Nigeria ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d62\"},\"ref\":\"d62\",\"snippet\":\" ... Chigozie Obioma, in The Orchestra of Minorities does the same. You shall notice in my next novel, The Wanderers [to be published in April/May], that I delve into this a little deeper also, to depict the notion of the absurdity of the human condition, which though popularized ... \",\"title\":\"https://africasacountry.com/2021/03/the-xhosa-literary-revival\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d65\"},\"ref\":\"d65\",\"snippet\":\" ... I loved your recent photos of everyday Nigeria. Your warmth and work will remain in our hearts. May God console your family.\\n\\nRichard Ali\\n\\nThis is such terrible news. Biyi Bandele grew up in a railway town closely related to the one I grew up in, and we ... \",\"title\":\"https://brittlepaper.com/2022/08/100-african-writers-celebrate-biyi-bandeles-life-and-work-2/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d94\"},\"ref\":\"d94\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2021-05-12\\n---\\nNigeria Football League 2016\\n\\nFederation Cup 2016\\n\\nFinal Table: 1.Enugu Rangers International FC 36 18 9 9 53-37 63 [1-0] Champions 2.Rivers United (Port Harcourt) 36 19 3 14 38-29 60 [*] [1-2] 3.Wikki Tourists FC (Bauchi) 36 16 ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.rsssf.org/tablesn/nig2016.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d95\"},\"ref\":\"d95\",\"snippet\":\" ... Guardian Books Nigeria Limited, 1988), pp. 60–67\\n* Ogwude, Sophia O., \\\"History and Ideology in Chimamanda Adichie's Fiction\\\", Tydskrif Vir Letterkunde, 48.1 (2011), 110–123. \\n* Okonjo, Kamene, \\\"The Dual-Sex Political System in Operation: Igbo Women and Community Politics in Midwestern Nigeria\\\", in Nancy Hafkin and ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Thing_Around_Your_Neck\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"ba3154cab715387b3f9542dca47172174b31ca17c7d73f2c45114fbb85d9750c\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"894b482bf31c822decd827f40c499810f00f368df542031e8892829690d27f69\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Chigozie Obioma grew up Akure Nigeria childhood\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_9ef4fe5a56b34c3d9bc8aac4"},{"content":"I have strong evidence for the key facts. Let me verify the final connection: Marlon James was born in Kingston, Jamaica (d86, d89), and I need to confirm Chigozie Obioma grew up in Akure. The d38 page says he was \"born in Akure\" but I need to confirm he grew up there. Let me also verify the Booker Prize was \"originally created in the 2000s\" — actually, the Man Booker Prize name was adopted in 2002 when Man Group became sponsor. Let me read the Marlon James Wikipedia page to confirm his birthplace and check the Booker Prize origin.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"ref\": \"d86\"}","name":"read"},"id":"call_c1aa1e66c0f04ca4aba8bf91","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Marlon James Wikipedia novelist born Kingston Jamaica biography\", \"Chigozie Obioma grew up Akure childhood hometown biography\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_d701907e80b849488e6f021a","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"evidence\":{\"document\":\"d86\",\"document_chars\":27013,\"end\":3000,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e2\",\"sha256\":\"fe7103588bdedb65d2bce58f2eb8dcf7f7fb7a5d81aff763760b9decd9a62ef5\",\"snapshot\":\"650b898f3eaa1e0d792c8f3b8578b301f5b2335c6ab971f106e6f9e7bc6aa0e3\",\"start\":0,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: King Yellowman\\nauthor: Garnette Cadogan photography by Marlon James\\ndate: 2025-01-01\\n---\\nClimbing quiet, verdant hills that lead to a house peeking over a rambunctious Kingston, I visit Winston Foster, popularly known by his stage name Yellowman, to discuss a musical career spent attracting the affection and ire of reggae fans. In the early eighties, after the death of Bob Marley, fans of Jamaican popular music were impatient for a new star that embodied Marley's rebel style and roots-reggae sound. What they got was Yellowman, an albino who delivered rebelliousness through an irreverent, comic, catchy style over an assertive new sound named dancehall. And although political concerns drove some of his songs, what most steered them was his ribald lyrics—termed \\\"slackness\\\" in Jamaica—which propelled him to global fame, and, perhaps, helped shift how some saw albinos. Often mistreated and made alien—scorned as if they were lepers whose condition were contagious—albinos were now, in Yellowman's songs, a sex symbol. \\\"Hi, my name is Yellowman. And in the ghetto they call me Mr. Sexy.\\\" So begins one song in which the albino toaster repeats the boast, \\\"Them a mad over me… girl a go crazy over me.\\\" Its bawdy flavor notwithstanding, the song uses humor to push against the borders of listeners' imagination. \\\"Albinos were never on the forefront of society,\\\" he tells me, as he speaks of using music to \\\"break down that barrier.\\\" In his voice was the defense, not only the pleasure, of many.\\n\\n\\\"I'm a soldier,\\\" Yellowman declares early in my visit, and repeats shortly before I leave, as if to bookend our conversation with an image he wants to inscribe in my memory. But he need not insist: it was his perseverance, his dogged resistance against obstacle after another, that brought me to his home. In 1984, as he jumped on the global stage, he was diagnosed with cancer and given a few years to live. Corrective surgery took away the tumor and a significant portion of his face, but seemingly none of his wit or fight. He's still here. Still here: that phrase, said to me with gumption and gratitude, had the ring of a mantra. \\\"I can't stop. I cannot stop. I don't see myself stopping because I grow with this in me, music. This talent is not influenced by anybody, this talent handed down to me by the Almighty.\\\" That's him, assuring me that he'll never stop performing, reinforcing his belief that music is bound up in his DNA, as if by divine fiat.\\n\\nIn performance, he is boundless energy—running, jumping, dancing,\\n\\neven doing pushups between songs—reminding us that he has not merely survived,\\n\\nbut that he is here to carry us along in his enthusiasms.\\n\\nIn performance, he is boundless energy—running, jumping, dancing, even doing pushups between songs—reminding us that he has not merely survived, but that he is here to carry us along in his enthusiasms. (\\\"When I tell them to jump, them jump. When I tell them to sing, them sing,\\\" he marvels to me, delighted and amazed th\"},\"executed\":true,\"next_start\":3000,\"ok\":true,\"previously_received\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_c1aa1e66c0f04ca4aba8bf91"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d89\"},\"ref\":\"d89\",\"snippet\":\" ... A Man on the Inside premieres 21 November on Netflix internationally\\n\\nGet Millie Black\\n\\nThe Jamaican-born novelist Marlon James, whose books include the Booker Prize winner A Brief History of Seven Killings (2014) and the Africa-set fantasy Black Leopard, Red Wolf (2019) created this crime series ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.bbc.com/culture/article/20241028-11-of-the-best-tv-shows-to-watch-this-november\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d90\"},\"ref\":\"d90\",\"snippet\":\" ... A Brief History of Seven Killings, by Marlon James\\n\\nA nightmare symphony of crime that begins in 1970s Jamaica and never really leaves, even as the semi-historical plot leaves a surreal blood trail from a Bob Marley assassination attempt to crack-addled New York City. James' intoxicating ... \",\"title\":\"https://ew.com/books/2019/11/25/best-of-the-decade-top-10-fiction-books/?srsltid=AfmBOop0ufKoVqU4RELY55P6eS3L4rXFZLCabqalM9VtLWkrcVEOOLAO\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d72\"},\"ref\":\"d72\",\"snippet\":\" ... Marlon James\\n\\nWinner of the prestigious Booker Prize in 2015 for his book A Brief History of Seven Killings, Marlon James is a Jamaican novelist and teacher of literature at Macalester College in St. Paul, Minnesota. Both his parents worked with the Jamaican police. His mother, a detective ... \",\"title\":\"https://medium.com/@smilodon207/what-music-do-celebrated-authors-listen-to-while-they-write-39f04ddf7f28\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d92\"},\"ref\":\"d92\",\"snippet\":\" ... Old Bill\\\"), born in Murree, India,1888.\\n\\n• George Baker, British Actor, born in Bulgaria\\n\\n• James.G. Ballard, British Fiction Writer, born in Shanghai, China,